SECTION 1 (new TCA 47-18-5603(a)): A financial institution shall not discriminate against a person solely on the basis that the person is lawfully engaged in commerce with respect to qualified products or against a trade association solely on the basis of its status as a trade association.
SECTION 1 (new TCA 47-18-5603(b)(1)): The refusal of a financial institution to provide financial services to a person or trade association;
SECTION 1 (new TCA 47-18-5604(a)(3)): Recover a civil penalty not to exceed ten thousand dollars ($10,000) for each violation of § 47-18-5603.
